      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "see the note to the last Stanza. Here it is used in its second",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "sense.—S'ikhariṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXVII.—यत्—तत् = since or seeing that—then. इन and भर्तृ",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "both are names of the Sun. III. Amarakosh, Nânârtha. विकृति in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "nearly the same sense as निकृति which itself occurs as a variant",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "here in some copies. It means something that is wrong, of-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "fence, injury. For विकृति comp. Uttararâmacharita 134 तदपि खलु मे स",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "व्याहारस्तुरङ्गमराक्षिणां ॥ विकृतिमखिलक्षत्राक्षेपप्रचण्डतयाकरोत । For निकृति com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "pare Kirâta I., 43 or III., 44. There is a double meaning in पाद,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "foot or ray. For the construction सहते standing for सहेत comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "Vîracharita pp. 75-24. Compare for the idea Uttararâmacharita p.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "148. मयूखैरश्रान्तं तपति यदि देवो दिनकरः ॥ किमाग्नेयग्रावा निकृत इव तेजांसि वमति.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "—Âryâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXVIII.—About the meaning of कपोलभित्ति see Malli-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "nâtha's commentary on Raghu. V., 43. For प्रकृति comp. Stanza",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "52. The idea of the last line finds frequent expression in Sanskṛit",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Literature ; तेजसा सह जातानां वयः कुत्रोपयुज्यते or Kâlidâsa's तेजसां हि न",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "वयः समीक्ष्यते, or Bhavabhûti's गुणाः पूजास्थानं गुणिषु न च लिङ्गं न च वयः are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "other well-known instances.—Âryâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XXXIX.—गच्छताम् which has been stated to be the read-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ing of most of the copies consulted is difficult of explanation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "grammatically, गम् by itself not being given in the grammars or",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "used in the literature as an Âtmaṇepadi root. अभिजन the commen-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "tator renders by स्वजन, but as all the other things enumerated are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "qualities residing in an individual, that meaning, even if allow-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "able elsewhere, is not admissible here. Here it means nobility",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "of birth as in S'âkuntala अभिजनवतो भर्तुः श्लाघ्ये स्थिता गृहिणीपदे and many",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "places besides. वैरिणि = अनुपकारिणि says Râmarshi. The positive mean-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "ing, however, is not bad.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XL.—अप्रतिहत = unrepulsed—a head which is at home in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "every subject. अर्थोष्मन् Compare Vîracharita p. 95 (शौर्योष्मन्) and",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
